---
// Fig. for "Finite Fields": the whole reason the field needs to be huge —
// GF(7) is small enough to search by hand, GF(BN254 prime) has roughly
// 2^254 elements, which is nowhere close to searchable.
---
<svg viewBox="0 0 680 210" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="width:100%;height:auto;display:block;">
  <line x1="340" y1="14" x2="340" y2="196" stroke="#223049" stroke-width="1" />

  <text x="170" y="46" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8fdcff" font-size="17" font-weight="800" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">GF(7)</text>
  <text x="170" y="98" text-anchor="middle" fill="#e9eef5" font-size="22" font-weight="800" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">7 elements</text>
  <text x="170" y="154" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ff8080" font-size="14.5" font-weight="800" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">&#10007; brute-forceable instantly</text>

  <text x="510" y="46" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8fdcff" font-size="17" font-weight="800" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">GF(BN254 prime)</text>
  <text x="510" y="98" text-anchor="middle" fill="#e9eef5" font-size="22" font-weight="800" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">&#8776; 2<tspan dy="-9" font-size="65%">254</tspan><tspan dy="9"> elements</tspan></text>
  <text x="510" y="154" text-anchor="middle" fill="#5ddc8a" font-size="14.5" font-weight="800" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">&#10003; computationally infeasible to search</text>
</svg>
